      "question": {
        ":question/id": "21d347ea-9600-5edd-8e03-478cdd2db340",
        ":question/problem": "Use the substitution $u=x^{2}$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int 3 \\cdot 3^{x^{2}} x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=x^{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2 x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 3 \\cdot 3^{x^{2}} x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int 3^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\left(\\int 3^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
