      "question": {
        ":question/id": "a4503e29-3b4f-54ed-b64a-d669140a8811",
        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 2 \\cdot 5^{x^{2} + 2} x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int 5^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{5^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=x^{2} + 2$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(2 x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 2 \\cdot 5^{x^{2} + 2} x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\int 5^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n\\int 5^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\frac{5^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5^{x^{2} + 2}}{\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}+C.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "bea41166-803e-5e0b-8045-a5fea638bee2",
