        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=2 - x^{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(- 3 x^{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 4 \\cdot 5^{2 - x^{3}} x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int 5^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\int 5^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\frac{5^{u}}{\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{4}{3}\\left(\\frac{5^{2 - x^{3}}}{\\ln{\\left(5 \\right)}}\\right)+C.\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
